            "time": "2026-11-17T19:21:37Z",
            "id": 104310,
            "is_private": false,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
            "text": "## Summary\n\nAfter an error in R code that a graphics device evaluates while drawing (a clipping path, mask, pattern or group function, for example), the device stays locked: `dev.off()` warns \"Killing locked device\" and `killDevice()` refuses to close it. Fixes a clear bug.\n\n## Details\n\n`lockDevice()` in `src/main/engine.c` sets `cend` before calling `begincontext()`, which resets it to `NULL`, so `clearLockFlag()` never runs on an error. `list.files()` and `list.dirs()` in `src/main/platform.c` make the same mistake and leak the path buffer when the traversal is interrupted. Tested on R-devel r90922.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `context-cleanup-order-repro.R`; it prints the warning from `dev.off()`, \"Killing locked device\", where none is expected.\n\nProposed patch: attached as `context-cleanup-order.diff`; it assigns the cleanup handlers after `begincontext()` and adds a regression test to `reg-tests-1e.R`.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/504, where CI results can be seen.",
            "bug_id": 19335,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "creator": "kevinushey",
